## Countdown Timer Requirements

* Must be **globally synced** across:

  * Landing page
  * /lane view
  * Admin-configured launch date
* Displays:

  * Days
  * Hours
  * Minutes
* State changes:

  * Pre-launch → “Opens Soon”
  * Live → “We’re Live”
  * Closed → “The Lane Has Closed”

---

## Visual Direction (Valentine’s)

### Allowed Adjustments

* Accent colors (soft reds, blush, charcoal, off-white)
* Seasonal imagery (romantic, thoughtful, gift-oriented)
* Typography emphasis (headlines only)

### Not Allowed

* Removing brand/category/CTA elements
* Adding gradients over images
* Cropping product imagery in a way that hides info
* Changing card logic or interactions

---

## Card Layout Rules (Lane View)

* All cards must show:

  * Brand name
  * Category
  * Offer text
  * Action buttons
* No gradient overlays on product images
* Images must not bleed into content areas
* Card height may increase to preserve readability
* Design must remain consistent across desktop & mobile

---

## Mobile Optimization (Mandatory)

* Cards must render fully without overlap
* Countdown must remain readable
* CTAs must be thumb-friendly
* No horizontal scrolling
* Typography must scale without truncation

---

## SEO & Discoverability

Minimum requirements for this rebrand:

* Updated meta title & description (Valentine’s Lane)
* Semantic HTML structure
* Accessible labels for countdown & CTAs
* Open Graph tags for social sharing
* Page speed prioritized (no heavy media)

---

## Lane Club (Community Continuity)

Valentine’s Lane continues to leverage **The Lane Club** as the community heartbeat.

